.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAD-LIST-EVENTS 1 "September 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.73" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-ead-list-events \- show the audit trail, newest first
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli ead list-events
[\fB\-\-user\fR|\fB\-u\fR \fIID\fR]
[\fB\-\-module\fR|\fB\-m\fR \fINAME\fR]
[\fB\-\-command\fR|\fB\-c\fR \fINAME\fR]
[\fB\-\-page\-size\fR|\fB\-s\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-page\-index\fR|\fB\-i\fR \fIN\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows what was run, by whom, in which account and namespace, with the
parameters the command carried and the status it was answered with.
.PP
Newest first, because that is the question people ask of an audit \-
"what just happened" \- and a trail paged oldest first would put the
answer on the last page.
.SH COLUMNS
.TP
.I accountId
The account the command was run in.
.TP
.I namespace
The namespace it was run in, empty for a command that names none.
.TP
.I userId
Who ran it, taken from the identity the gateway verified and never from
the request body. A record of who did something that the doer can write
is not a record of anything.
.TP
.I module
The module the command was addressed to, e.g.
.IR esm .
.TP
.I command
The command, e.g.
.IR delete-bucket .
.TP
.I parameters
What it was called with, with sensitive values replaced \- see
.BR euclid-cli-ead (1).
.TP
.I status
The HTTP status it was answered with.
.I 403
is a refusal, and is the entry the trail is kept for.
.TP
.I created
When it happened.
.SH FILTERS
Each is optional and they combine. The account is not among them: every
read is confined to the caller's own, whatever is asked for.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-user " " \fIID\fR
Only this user.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-module " " \fINAME\fR
Only this module, e.g.
.IR esm .
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-command " " \fINAME\fR
Only this command, e.g.
.IR delete-bucket .
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-page\-size " " \fIN\fR
How many entries per page. Default 10.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-page\-index " " \fIN\fR
Which page. Default 0.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
A page
.RI ( "{events, total}" )
is printed as JSON.
.I total
is how many the filter matches, not how many are on the page.
.TP
.B 1
The caller was not authenticated, or does not hold
.IR ead:list-events .
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
# What has happened recently
euclid-cli ead list-events

# What one person did, fifty at a time
euclid-cli ead list-events --user jvo --page-size 50

# Every bucket deletion, whoever made it
euclid-cli ead list-events --module esm --command delete-bucket

# Second page of one module's entries
euclid-cli ead list-events --module eqs --page-size 20 --page-index 1
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-ead (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ead-count-events (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ead-purge-events (1)
